# rrubocop

10x faster RuboCop drop-in for Ruby (tree-sitter). Same CLI, configs, and output — no RuboCop gems to maintain.

## Layout
- `src/cli.rs` — RuboCop-compatible CLI (`--mcp` starts MCP server)
- `src/mcp/` — MCP stdio server via official `rmcp` (`offense`, `tools`; `rubocop_inspection` / `rubocop_autocorrection`)
- `src/baseline.rs` + `src/resources/baseline.json` — RuboCop/gem versions for `--help`/`--version`
- `src/resources/gem_configs/` + `gem_configs_manifest.json` (+ optional `same_as` identical-YAML aliases) + `scripts/fetch_gem_configs.py` — vendored public gem YAML (by version from GitHub) compiled in via `build.rs`; `Gemfile.lock` selects version / alias; parsed in memory
- `src/config/` — RuboCop-parity YAML (`mod.rs` re-exports; `gem_path`/`gem_path_local`/`gem_path_version`/`gem_configs` — embed first, else `bundle info --path` for private/unlisted gems, `yaml_read` ERB (native simple-ERB: literals/vars/`ENV`; ruby fallback), `types`, `globutil`, `filter`/`filter_match`/`filter_path`, `discover` (incl. `~/.rubocop.yml` / XDG fallback), `standard`/`standard_convert`, `merge`/`merge_cop`, `parse`/`parse_{allcops,cop}`, `load`/`load_{defaults,require,gems,recursive,lockfile,resolve}`, `ruby_ver`, `resolved`/`resolved_{state,enabled,inject,cop_cfg,filters,effective,fingerprint}`)
- `src/cache/` — abcop-style redb result cache (`RRUBOCOP_CACHE_DIR` / XDG)
- `src/cop/` — cops by department (`bundler`, `factory_bot`(+association_style), `gemspec`(+ordered_dependencies_group), `graphql`(+helpers/{args,kwargs,description,names_field,klass,names}; 26 cops), `layout` (91 Layout cops incl. `line_length`), `lint` (71, incl. `empty_file` + `unused_method_argument` + `constant_definition_in_block` + `redundant_require_statement` + `useless_access_modifier/` + `format_parameter_mismatch/`), `metrics` (+`class_length`/`module_length`), `naming`, `performance`, `rails`, `rake`, `rspec`(+helpers), `rspec_rails`(+inferred_spec_type), `security`, `style` (143 Style cops + `heuristics/` {percent,string_literals,…} + `trailing_comma_args`), `shared`, `walker`, `registry`)
- `src/fs.rs` — file discover; `AllCops.Exclude` via CopFilterSet (RuboCop `-L`)
- `src/parse/` — SourceFile, CodeMap, directives, tree-sitter parse
- `src/linter/` — parallel lint + cache (`mod.rs`, `parallel.rs`) and per-file phases (`engine/` + `syntax_gate`); line/source opt-in, shared `FileModel` for variable/metrics cops, single AST `BatchedWalker` by `interested_node_kinds` (+ optional `interested_call_names` gate for `call`/`command`/`command_call`); `CodeMap` built once in source phase only when plain source cops run (syntax gate uses empty map)
- `src/formatter/` — text/json/progress (live marks)/…
- `src/abc/`, `src/model/` — Metrics/AbcSize (tree-sitter); bare `super` marks method params (`IntroKind::Param`); `binding` marks all locals
- `vendor/tree-sitter-ruby/` — grammar
- `testdata/cross_test_nitrocop.py` — offense compare vs local nitrocop
- `testdata/cross_test_rubocop.py` (+ `_json` / `_cmp`) — offense compare vs `bundle exec rubocop` (skips if unavailable)
- `tests/fixtures/cops/` — nitrocop-style `offense.rb` / `no_offense.rb` per cop (`src/testutil/` + `cop_fixture_tests!`); when fixing FPs/parity, always add fixtures (see `.cursor/rules/cop-parity-tests.mdc`)
- Reference clones (outside repo): local `nitrocop`, `rubocop`, `abcop` checkouts (set `NITROCOP` for `testdata/cross_test_nitrocop.py`)
- Parity on external projects: compare against `bundle exec rubocop` (project Gemfile), not bare `rubocop` from PATH — see `.cursor/rules/cop-parity-tests.mdc`
- CI (`ci.yml`): `cargo test --locked` + [abcop](https://github.com/adrianov/abcop) `--full` (pinned `.deb` from Releases; AbcSize ≤17 / ModuleAbcSize ≤120; no Rust disable directives — split modules / extract fns)
- Publish (`publish.yml`): tag `v*` → crates.io + Ubuntu 22.04 `.deb` + macOS `.tar.gz` GitHub Release; Homebrew tap `adrianov/rrubocop`
- `.cursor/rules/abcop-diff-review.mdc` — before finishing code changes: `abcop --full` (AbcSize ≤17, ModuleAbcSize ≤120; refactor, no disables) + `git diff -w -W --histogram --no-prefix` for semantic review; smallest correct diff
- `.cursor/rules/squash-merge-prs.mdc` — auto squash-merge every ready PR after `ci`, then delete the head branch; `.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml` lands them (do not `gh pr merge --auto` here — no required checks)
